# The old-channel thread and the injury rescue. Arc, owners and plants:
# content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.
# Thread owners (`who ow_*`) are cast once per voyage and never overlap.

card m_carrier
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 15 19
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when !is A ow_dose
text {A}'s arrival-test dish scans the old common channel toward Mars; no one has listened there since the relay was written off. A week of integration shows a faint carrier. Folded at 10.96 seconds, 2.4 percent duty, it stands up like a fence post. "An alias, probably," {A} says.
do who ow_hail A
do mark t_carrier

card m_alias
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 20 21
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when since t_carrier >= 4
when fired m_theory
text {A} asks {B} to point a second dish at the carrier. The bursts land on both in the same millisecond and slide against a fixed 10.96-second clock by over a second and a half a day, the fleet's closing rate on Mars. Hour to hour the residuals stay flat. "Booked again. Out," {A} logs.
do bond A B 3
do open dec_signal

card dec_signal
type decision
cat mystery
days 20 23
weight 1
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious open log
when fired m_alias
when is A ow_hail
text If it's the grey relay, it may still know a standard hello. {A} wants clearance to answer every burst with one, signed with the old program key the fleet carries as a relay fallback: a courtesy, and a test. {B} points out that every reply ties up the comms computer.
option open | Answer every burst | The ground clears it inside a day: hello only, nothing that commands, inhibits set from the ground. The first hello goes out at 14:02, timed to the millisecond. {B} files one line of dissent, signed, and leaves it there.
  set signal_answered
  morale B -3
  trait A curious 5
option log | File it, keep going | The carrier goes into the anomaly file under "later". {A} files a signed dissent; {B} countersigns it.
  set signal_ignored
  morale A -5

card signal_reply
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 25 26
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when is A ow_hail
do mark t_frame
text Stacked over a week of bursts, the receiver pulls out half a frame of housekeeping on the old channel, cut off partway. One field is a counter, up twenty-seven thousand and change in a week. {A} logs the figure under the date of the first hello, no remark beside it. "Counter noted. Out."
do trait A curious 4

card signal_echo
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 25 27
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
do mark t_frame
text Folding a week of noise, {A} finds half a frame of housekeeping on the old channel, cut off partway. Its period hasn't moved by a millisecond in a day. One field is a counter that hasn't moved since the scrap before. Whatever it counts, nothing has given it one.
do morale A -3

# Injury and rescue: needs supplies from another ship.
card c_hail
type beat
cat mystery
due
once
days 39 39
roles A
when is A ow_hail
text Close to half a million knocks heard since the first, every gap explained: Mars in the way, a cold night. Last night's cold gap ran forty, and the knock after it came in a decibel weaker. {A} adds the point and the line steepens: the beat runs out a few nights after landing, not weeks. "Noted. Out."
do trait A curious 1

card crisis_eva
type event
cat grim
once
days 10 34
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
when kit_elsewhere A
when !is A cam_who
text On {A}'s scheduled EVA a tether snags on a bracket and wrenches {A}'s arm, with the next ship closed up and a suited crewmate clipped in at its hatch. {A} frees it, works back along the line hand over hand, and comes inside with a wrist that won't bend.
do cond A injured
do who eva_who A
do morale A -10
do open rescue_kit

card rescue_kit
type rescue
cat grim
duration 1
roles A B
default volunteer
when cond A injured
when apart B A
text {A} needs the ultrasound probe from another ship's medical kit, and the next scheduled crossing window is days away.
option send | Send the kit | The kit rides the line across alone. {A}'s wrist is scanned and splinted by lunch, and the anomaly report runs to four pages.
  kit A
  res fuel -1
  morale A 6
option volunteer | {B} brings it over | {B} rides the line across with the kit and splints the wrist personally. The report calls it "nominal". Seven ships read it, and every one of them knows better.
  kitfrom B A
  move B A
  res fuel -1
  bond A B 12
  morale B 4

